        </div>

        <svg class="about-moon" viewBox="0 0 400 400" data-drift="70" data-scale="0.08" data-rotate="2" data-pointer="10" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M 300 60 A 150 150 0 1 0 300 340 A 138 138 0 0 1 300 60 Z" />
        </svg>

        <div class="section-content">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker"><span class="kicker-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span> About</p>
            <h2 id="about-title" class="section-title">Curious about how complex systems hold together.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="section-body section-body--narrow">
            <div class="prose-night">
              <p>
                I am Ahmad Zulkarnaen, a full-stack and mobile developer working between Bogor and Karawang, Indonesia. Most of what I build is end to end: a Laravel or REST backend, a Next.js interface, a Flutter app in someone's pocket.
              </p>
              <p>
                Away from the editor I spend a lot of time outside after dark, and the rest with whichever cat has found the warmest chair. This page is the quiet side of my work. The history, the projects, and the code live in Elsewhere.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 02: Principles -->
      <section id="principles" class="section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
        <svg class="celestial celestial--planet" viewBox="0 0 120 80" data-drift="110" data-scale="0.12" data-rotate="5" data-pointer="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <ellipse cx="60" cy="40" rx="50" ry="11" transform="rotate(-18 60 40)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.22" />
          <circle cx="60" cy="40" r="25" fill="rgba(184,198,217,0.03)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.28" />
        </svg>

        <div class="section-cat-flyer section-cat-flyer--right section-cat-flyer--principles" data-side="right" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="cat-float-wrap">
            <div class="cat-float-inner">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="/cats/cat-4.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img class="section-cat-img" src="/cats/cat-4.svg" alt="" width="1389" height="1411" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section-content">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker"><span class="kicker-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span> Principles</p>
            <h2 id="principles-title" class="section-title">How I try to work.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="section-body">
            <ol class="principle-list">
              <li class="principle">
                <span class="principle__index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                <div class="principle__body">
                  <h3 class="principle__title">Readable over clever.</h3>
                  <p class="principle__text">If a line needs a comment to explain why it is smart, it is usually the wrong line. I write for the person who opens the file next, who is often me in six months.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="principle">
                <span class="principle__index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
                <div class="principle__body">
                  <h3 class="principle__title">Keep the boring parts boring.</h3>
                  <p class="principle__text">Auth, migrations, and deploys should be predictable. The interesting effort belongs in the product, not in a homemade way to do what the framework already does well.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="principle">
                <span class="principle__index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
                <div class="principle__body">
                  <h3 class="principle__title">Watch it after release.</h3>
                  <p class="principle__text">The launch is a moment. The ordinary Tuesday is the test. I care about logs, empty states, and the small edges that only appear once people use the thing.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 03: Notes -->
      <section id="notes" class="section" aria-labelledby="notes-title">
        <svg class="celestial celestial--planet-small" viewBox="0 0 64 64" data-drift="150" data-scale="0.16" data-rotate="-8" data-pointer="26" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <defs>
            <radialGradient id="planet-small-fill" cx="35%" cy="30%" r="70%">
              <stop offset="0" stop-color="rgba(238,242,246,0.18)" />
              <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="rgba(73,108,167,0.10)" />
              <stop offset="1" stop-color="rgba(11,16,32,0.05)" />
            </radialGradient>
          </defs>
